{"tool_name":"hotspot_sperm-typing_","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"hotspot_sperm-typing_","home":"http://github.com/evolbioinf/hotspot/","license":"GPL-2.0","summary":"Software to support sperm-typing for investigating recombination hotspots.","addition_date":"2019-08-04T09:55:15Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T21:06:18.225174Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:hotspot_sperm-typing_","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"haubold@evolbio.mpg.de","name":"Bernhard Haubold","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/EvolBioInf/hotspot/blob/master/README.md"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"PCR primer design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0308"},{"term":"Recombination detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0451"},{"term":"SNP detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0484"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"hotspot","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"Ruta","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btw195","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: In many organisms, including humans, recombination clusters within recombination hotspots. The standard method for de novo detection of recombinants at hotspots is sperm typing. This relies on allele-specific PCR at single nucleotide polymorphisms. Designing allele-specific primers by hand is time-consuming. We have therefore written a package to support hotspot detection and analysis. Results: hotspot consists of four programs: asp looks up SNPs and designs allele-specific primers; aso constructs allele-specific oligos for mapping recombinants; xov implements a maximum-likelihood method for estimating the crossover rate; six, finally, simulates typing data.","authors":[{"name":"Dutheil J.Y."},{"name":"Haubold B."},{"name":"Klotzl F."},{"name":"Odenthal-Hesse L."}